A smartphone comparison and specifications database website for tech buyers, called [your site name]. The site helps visitors compare phones by price, camera, battery, RAM, storage, 5G/NFC support, processor, and display specs. Include a homepage highlighting popular and trending phones, a searchable/filterable phone listing page, individual detail pages for each phone model, and a comparison tool to compare two or more phones side by side. Also include a blog section for phone reviews and buying guides, an About page, a Contact page, and a Privacy Policy page. Clean, modern tech/gadget design with a blue and white color scheme, card-based layouts for phone listings, and a professional, trustworthy feel suitable for a content and advertising-supported site."
A few notes on what happens next:
The AI builder will generate a template structure with placeholder phones — it won't know your actual 997-phone dataset. After it builds the skeleton, you'll need to get your real data into it, which for WordPress usually means a plugin (like WP All Import or a custom post type + CSV importer) to bulk-load your CSV as phone entries.
If the builder gives you a generic/thin site, ask it (or use "Enhance with AI") to expand: more detail fields per phone, a comparison table layout, related-phones suggestions — these matter for both UX and AdSense approval.
Don't forget to keep the Privacy Policy and About/Contact pages it generates — AdSense checks for these.
